  "generationStage": "R1-b on the amendment 19 tree (candidate #80 + R1-a + R2-a + R2-b + R3-a at 77175d85): the opening life of Act I (m01-opening.js; mission.json openingLife): every Polish man near the player's opening route has a state-driven activity of his own from the first tick (a weighted plan per tension, calm / warned / planes, held for a time drawn from his own stream, never the same act twice running, a reaction delay of his own to a change of tension), the runner pl_west_1 carries the sergeant's word along the line by the simulation's A* walk (his errands are mission data, each man he tells is on alert at once), the sapper team walks the cable and kneels at a joint (always kneeling when still, so the staging invariant holds), Nowicki's run for the sappers starts 5 s after the planes are heard, the planes make every man react and the first bomb ends the record; the garrison stands on its posts to the bit when the bombs fall (the runner and the sappers arrive exactly on their places), the facing is written when the act's wish changes, no draw from any random stream; saved as the optional validated record timers.opening and the optional validated actor.act (a save from before has neither and gets them at the next tick; the first bomb removes both); the rearguard's and Kowal's npc-shot events carry end / hit (presentation: the long-range impact FX draws them); five new reactive lines on the new `opening` trigger of the director (dlg_m01_210..212 and the callouts co_m01_opening_order / co_m01_opening_alert, Polish by an AI author, to be reviewed by a native speaker); golden amendment 20",
